      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-143530",
      ":question/problem": "A math teacher splits her calculus class into three groups such that $35%$ of all the students are in Group A, $35%$ are in Group B, and $30%$ are in Group C. If $20%$ of the students in Group A obtained the top grade, $10%$ in Group B obtained the top grade, and the probability that a randomly selected student from any group obtained the top grade is $0.255$, what is the probability that a randomly selected student from Group C obtained the top grade?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
