      ":question/problem": "At a gas station, $40%$ of the customers buy Regular gasoline, $45%$ buy Premium gasoline, and $15%$ buy Supreme gasoline. It is known that $65%$ of the customers who purchase Regular gasoline and $50%$ of the customers who buy Premium gasoline pay with a credit card. If the probability that a randomly selected customer pays with a credit card is $57.5%,$ what percentage of Supreme gasoline customers pay using a credit card?"
